  "declienting": [
    "Modeled the accepted responsive native-select behavior as the governed native-select structural variant under the existing Tabs canonical.",
    "Reused the default Tabs selection, ID, roving-focus, keyboard, tablist, and panel primitives so both responsive controls operate one interaction engine and one panel tree.",
    "Kept browser access inside a client effect and limited it to matchMedia focus transfer when the focused responsive copy becomes display-hidden at lg.",
    "Required plain-text item labels for valid native option content while leaving the default Tabs ReactNode label API unchanged.",
    "Rejected CMS placeholders, editor warnings, content filtering, label-service resolution, and application orchestration."
  ],
